From 846dfa0758df267e0404508bfafd67e44f819961 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeiroNext <mihail.rozshko@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 12:42:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Place tasks with only a due date; release +unity2 (LP:
 #1848969, #2099742)

A task without DTSTART (as Nextcloud Tasks creates them) left the
appointment's begin unset, and formatting it for a debug message aborted
the service in DateTime::get(). Use the due date for such a task, and
leave out a component without any time. Test: test-eds-ics-tasks-without-start.

Assisted-by: LLM claude-opus-5-5
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 debian/changelog                              | 11 +++
 src/engine-eds.cpp                            | 24 +++--
 tests/CMakeLists.txt                          |  1 +
 tests/test-eds-ics-tasks-without-start.cpp    | 87 +++++++++++++++++++
 tests/test-eds-ics-tasks-without-start.ics.in | 25 ++++++
 5 files changed, 143 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 tests/test-eds-ics-tasks-without-start.cpp
 create mode 100644 tests/test-eds-ics-tasks-without-start.ics.in

diff --git a/debian/changelog b/debian/changelog
index 3252176..d2ce45d 100644
--- a/debian/changelog
+++ b/debian/changelog
@@ -1,3 +1,14 @@
+indicator-datetime (15.10+21.04.20210304-0ubuntu6+unity2) resolute; urgency=medium
+
+  * src/engine-eds.cpp: a task with only a due date (as Nextcloud Tasks
+    creates them) has no DTSTART, so its begin time stayed unset and
+    formatting it for a debug message aborted the service in
+    DateTime::get() (LP: #1848969, #2099742). Place such a task at its due
+    date, and leave out a component that has no time at all.
+  * tests: add test-eds-ics-tasks-without-start.
+
+ -- Ubuntu Unity Life Support <mihail.rozshko@gmail.com>  Sat, 26 Sep 2026 12:23:34 +0000
+
 indicator-datetime (15.10+21.04.20210304-0ubuntu6+unity1) resolute; urgency=medium
 
